  },
  {
    "id": "57e36464-9183-4f90-8822-07b5921adc8d",
    "title": "Embroidery Patch",
    "prompt": "Convert the photo into a stitched embroidery patch, preserving the person's pose, facial features, hairstyle, and clothing silhouette so they remain clearly recognizable within the constraints of embroidered thread art. Render every surface using visible thread texture — dense, directional satin stitches for larger areas, fine detail stitching for facial features, and slightly raised, fuzzy fiber texture throughout, as if machine-embroidered onto felt or twill fabric. Use a simplified, moderately saturated color palette suited to embroidery thread (avoid ultra-fine gradients; blend color transitions with visible stitch-direction changes instead). Outline the entire figure with a bold embroidered border stitch, and give the whole image a rounded or scalloped patch-shaped edge with a visible fabric-colored border, as if it's a sew-on patch. Add a couple of small decorative embroidered elements in the background echoing the original setting (simple stitched shapes, no readable text) kept subordinate to the main figure. Preserve the person's recognizable pose and features throughout. Do not generate: smooth photographic texture, flat vector coloring, 3D rendering, painterly brushwork, or loss of the person's recognizable identity.",
    "identityMode": "reinforced",
    "imageFile": "3579a16f-7dfc-4907-85dd-633e99003ce6.jpg",
