  {
    "id": "e357d177-3c0a-4d2f-9638-4bd0d6462086",
    "title": "Cross-Stitch Pattern",
    "prompt": "Convert the photo into a cross-stitch embroidery pattern, preserving the person's pose, facial features, hairstyle, and clothing silhouette so they remain clearly recognizable. Render the entire image as a grid of small, uniform X-shaped stitches, each a single flat color, visible individually like a charted needlepoint pattern stitched onto even-weave fabric. Use a limited, blocky color palette with hard-edged transitions between colors rather than smooth gradients, since each stitch can only hold one color. Keep the aida-cloth fabric texture visible in the background and between stitches, with a slightly frayed or looped thread texture on close inspection. Keep the overall image charmingly pixelated and handcrafted-looking, like a real finished cross-stitch piece in an embroidery hoop or frame. Preserve the person's recognizable identity, pose, and features throughout, simplified into the stitch grid. Do not generate: smooth photographic gradients, painterly shading, a fully solid-fill embroidered patch with no visible stitch grid, or loss of the person's recognizable identity.",
    "identityMode": "reinforced",
    "categoryId": "6ad0a676-4347-4eb6-9db1-7b3938f373ae",
